  |title Penny-wise, pound-foolish

  |quote
    Did you really save crucial tokens by not reading the last several lines of those commit messages? once again, penny-wise, pound-foolish.

  |occasion
    After four commit bodies had been truncated with `head -6`, and the truncated
    remainder turned out to hold a corpus's design intent, a porting map, and two
    undocumented format defects.

  |about
    The economy that was never computed. The tell is that the efficiency story
    arrives afterward, when challenged.

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You are about to type `head -n`, `tail -n`, `--oneline`, `--stat`, or `wc -l` against a primary.
    - You are about to read a summary of something you could read.

  |see
    #ver-discount-is-unquestioning
